<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<mxfile host="app.diagrams.net">
  <diagram name="Acceptance Criteria — Increment 5" id="ac-increment-5">
    <mxGraphModel dx="0" dy="0" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="10900" pageHeight="900" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />
<mxCell id="inc5-game-state-queries-2" value="Game State Queries" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="20" y="20" width="970" height="519" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-query-hovered-npc-info-from-game-3" value="Query Hovered NPC Info from Game" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="125.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-query-hovered-npc-info-from-game-ac1-4" value="1. WHEN the GM&apos;s mouse pointer hovers over a visible NPC entity in the COH game viewport THEN the application invokes the Game State Query via the Game Bridge DLL AND the Hovered NPC Info (NPC name and identity) is returned and made available to the caller" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="35" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-query-hovered-npc-info-from-game-ac2-5" value="2. WHEN the GM&apos;s mouse is not hovering over any NPC entity in the game viewport THEN the Game State Query returns an empty Hovered NPC Info result BUT no error is raised and the calling service receives the empty signal without failure" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="35" y="206" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-query-hovered-npc-info-from-game-ac3-6" value="3. WHEN the Game Bridge is not initialized or the COH game client is not running THEN the Game State Query returns an unavailable signal to the caller BUT no NPC name or identity data is fabricated or returned as valid" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="35" y="288" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-query-hovered-npc-info-from-game-ac4-7" value="4. WHEN the GM moves the mouse from one NPC to another in the game viewport THEN the Hovered NPC Info updates to reflect the NPC now under the cursor AND the previous NPC&apos;s data is discarded; only the current hover target is returned" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="35" y="370" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-query-hovered-npc-info-from-game-ac5-8" value="5. WHEN the Hovered NPC Info is queried in rapid succession by the application THEN each query returns the NPC under the cursor at the time of that query call BUT no query blocks subsequent queries; each returns independently and promptly" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="35" y="452" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-query-mouse-xyz-position-in-game-world-9" value="Query Mouse XYZ Position in Game World" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="445.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-query-mouse-xyz-position-in-game-world-ac1-10" value="1. WHEN the application requests the Mouse XYZ Position THEN the Game State Query calls the Game Bridge DLL and returns the world-space X/Y/Z coordinate triple of the mouse cursor&apos;s current position in the COH game world AND the returned coordinates are immediately available for use in placement operations" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="355" y="110" width="300" height="100" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-query-mouse-xyz-position-in-game-world-ac2-11" value="2. WHEN the COH game window does not have input focus at the time of the query THEN the Game State Query returns the Mouse XYZ Position but marks it as potentially stale BUT no coordinates are silently treated as authoritative when focus is absent" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="355" y="220" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-query-mouse-xyz-position-in-game-world-ac3-12" value="3. WHEN the Game Bridge is unavailable THEN the Mouse XYZ Position query returns an unavailable signal BUT no zero-coordinate result is returned as if it were a valid world position" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="355" y="316" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-query-mouse-xyz-position-in-game-world-ac4-13" value="4. WHEN the GM positions the mouse at different in-game locations THEN each Mouse XYZ Position query returns distinct coordinates corresponding to each mouse placement AND the coordinates reflect the full three dimensions of the game world at that cursor point" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="355" y="398" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-check-game-done-state-14" value="Check Game Done State" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="765.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-check-game-done-state-ac1-15" value="1. WHEN the application polls the Game Done State and the COH session is still active THEN the Game State Query returns false AND no Roster Entry is affected and the Desktop Overlay remains unchanged" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="675" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-check-game-done-state-ac2-16" value="2. WHEN the Game Done State becomes true (map unload, disconnect, or client shutdown) THEN the Game State Query returns true AND all Roster Entries have their Spawned State set to false AND all Character Overlays are removed from the Desktop Overlay" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="675" y="192" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-check-game-done-state-ac3-17" value="3. WHEN Game Done State is true THEN no spawn, move, or other game command is issued until a new game session is established BUT the Roster entries themselves are preserved; only Spawned State is cleared" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="675" y="288" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-check-game-done-state-ac4-18" value="4. WHEN a new game session is established after Game Done State was true THEN the Game Done State flag is reset to false AND the GM may begin spawning characters from the Roster again" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="675" y="370" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-check-game-done-state-ac5-19" value="5. WHEN the application cannot reach the Game Bridge to poll Game Done State THEN the application treats the state as indeterminate and suspends game commands BUT the Roster and its Roster Entries are not cleared" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="675" y="438" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-game-command-infrastructure-20" value="Game Command Infrastructure" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1020" y="20" width="970" height="491" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-split-oversized-command-chains-for-execution-21" value="Split Oversized Command Chains for Execution" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1125.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-split-oversized-command-chains-for-execution-ac1-22" value="1. WHEN the application assembles a Command Chain for delivery THEN the payload size and command count are measured against the known COH engine limit before delivery is attempted" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1035" y="110" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-split-oversized-command-chains-for-execution-ac2-23" value="2. WHEN the Command Chain is within the COH limit THEN it is delivered to the Game Bridge as a single batch AND the COH engine processes all commands in the stated order" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1035" y="178" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-split-oversized-command-chains-for-execution-ac3-24" value="3. WHEN the Command Chain constitutes an Oversized Command Chain THEN it is split into two or more sub-chains, each within the COH limit AND each sub-chain is delivered to the Game Bridge in sequence, completing one before the next begins AND no command from the original chain is omitted or reordered" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1035" y="246" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-split-oversized-command-chains-for-execution-ac4-25" value="4. WHEN splitting is required and one sub-chain delivery fails THEN the application surfaces a delivery-error signal and does not attempt the remaining sub-chains BUT sub-chains already delivered are not reversed; commands already executed remain in effect" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1035" y="342" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-split-oversized-command-chains-for-execution-ac5-26" value="5. WHEN splitting would produce a sub-chain of zero commands THEN that sub-chain is not delivered BUT subsequent non-empty sub-chains are still delivered in order" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1035" y="438" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-close-game-bridge-on-shutdown-27" value="Close Game Bridge on Shutdown" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1445.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-close-game-bridge-on-shutdown-ac1-28" value="1. WHEN the GM closes the application or triggers application shutdown THEN the Game Bridge close sequence is initiated before the process exits AND all active DLL handles and HookCostume connections are released AND the Game State Query poll loop is stopped" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1355" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-close-game-bridge-on-shutdown-ac2-29" value="2. WHEN the Game Bridge close sequence completes THEN no further game commands are issued AND the application process exits cleanly without leaving orphaned DLL resources" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1355" y="206" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-close-game-bridge-on-shutdown-ac3-30" value="3. WHEN the Game Bridge is already in an uninitialized state at shutdown THEN the close sequence completes without error BUT no attempt is made to release handles that were never acquired" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1355" y="274" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-close-game-bridge-on-shutdown-ac4-31" value="4. WHEN the application crashes unexpectedly without a normal shutdown THEN COH-side Spawned NPCs remain in game (no implicit despawn on abnormal exit) BUT the HookCostume DLL is unloaded by the OS process cleanup" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1355" y="342" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-execute-load-map-command-32" value="Execute Load Map Command" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1765.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-execute-load-map-command-ac1-33" value="1. WHEN the GM triggers a Load Map action for a designated COH map THEN the Game Bridge issues the load-map slash command with the specified map identifier AND the COH client begins transitioning to the designated map" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1675" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-execute-load-map-command-ac2-34" value="2. WHEN the map transition completes in the COH client THEN the Game Done State is polled to confirm the new session is active AND the application proceeds with the new session state" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1675" y="192" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-execute-load-map-command-ac3-35" value="3. WHEN the specified map identifier is invalid or unavailable in COH THEN the Game Bridge issues the command and the COH engine rejects it AND the application receives an error signal and surfaces feedback to the GM BUT no application state is modified as a result of the failed map load" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1675" y="260" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-execute-load-map-command-ac4-36" value="4. WHEN the Game Bridge is not initialized when the Load Map action is triggered THEN the command is not issued AND the GM sees that the map load cannot proceed without an active game session" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1675" y="356" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-manage-pop-up-menus-37" value="Manage Pop-Up Menus" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2020" y="20" width="970" height="465" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-write-pop-up-menu-files-to-coh-menus-directory-38" value="Write Pop-Up Menu Files to COH Menus Directory" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2125.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-write-pop-up-menu-files-to-coh-menus-directory-ac1-39" value="1. WHEN the application writes a Pop-Up Menu THEN the menu definition text file is written to the COH Menus Directory AND the file is immediately available on disk for a subsequent load command" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2035" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-write-pop-up-menu-files-to-coh-menus-directory-ac2-40" value="2. WHEN a Pop-Up Menu file already exists at the target path in the COH Menus Directory THEN it is overwritten with the new content AND the most recently written version is the one the game will load on the next load command" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2035" y="192" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-write-pop-up-menu-files-to-coh-menus-directory-ac3-41" value="3. WHEN the COH Menus Directory does not exist or is not writable THEN the write fails and the application surfaces an error to the GM BUT no partial file is left in the directory" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2035" y="274" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-write-pop-up-menu-files-to-coh-menus-directory-ac4-42" value="4. WHEN the write succeeds THEN the written file path is confirmed and the application is ready to issue a load-pop-up-menu command BUT the COH game client does not automatically pick up the file until a load command is explicitly issued" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2035" y="342" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-load-pop-up-menu-in-game-43" value="Load Pop-Up Menu in Game" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2445.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-load-pop-up-menu-in-game-ac1-44" value="1. WHEN the application issues the load-pop-up-menu command for a named Pop-Up Menu THEN the Game Bridge delivers the command to the COH client AND the COH client loads the menu definition and makes its entries accessible from the in-game HUD" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2355" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-load-pop-up-menu-in-game-ac2-45" value="2. WHEN the load command is issued before the Pop-Up Menu file has been written to the COH Menus Directory THEN the COH client attempts the load and fails silently or produces a COH-side error AND the application surfaces a warning that the menu file must be written before loading" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2355" y="192" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-load-pop-up-menu-in-game-ac3-46" value="3. WHEN the COH client is not running when the load command is issued THEN the Game Bridge reports an unavailable signal BUT no menu state in the application is changed" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2355" y="288" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-load-pop-up-menu-in-game-ac4-47" value="4. WHEN the same Pop-Up Menu is loaded a second time after an update THEN the COH client replaces the previously loaded menu version with the updated one AND the new entries are immediately active in the game HUD" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2355" y="356" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-deploy-area-attack-pop-up-menu-48" value="Deploy Area Attack Pop-Up Menu" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2765.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-deploy-area-attack-pop-up-menu-ac1-49" value="1. WHEN a game session is initialized THEN the Area Attack Pop-Up Menu file is written to the COH Menus Directory AND the load-pop-up-menu command is issued via the Game Bridge to activate it in the COH client AND the area attack target designation entries become accessible from the COH HUD" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2675" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-deploy-area-attack-pop-up-menu-ac2-50" value="2. WHEN the write or load step fails during session initialization THEN the application surfaces a warning that the Area Attack Pop-Up Menu is unavailable AND the rest of the session initialization continues; area attack designation from the HUD is simply unavailable until the menu is deployed" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2675" y="206" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-deploy-area-attack-pop-up-menu-ac3-51" value="3. WHEN the Area Attack Pop-Up Menu is already deployed from a prior session start and the file is unchanged THEN the application writes the file again and reloads it to ensure the current session has the active version BUT the overwrite and reload do not cause errors if the menu content is identical" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2675" y="302" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-deploy-area-attack-pop-up-menu-ac4-52" value="4. WHEN the GM designates an area attack center target from within the COH game HUD THEN the Area Attack Pop-Up Menu entries are present and respond as defined AND the attack configuration panel in the application receives the center target designation" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="2675" y="398" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-populate-roster-53" value="Populate Roster" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3020" y="20" width="1610" height="519" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-add-character-to-roster-54" value="Add Character to Roster" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3125.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-add-character-to-roster-ac1-55" value="1. WHEN the GM adds a Character to the Roster via the Add action in the Roster Panel THEN a new Roster Entry is created for that character with Spawned State false and no active or gang indicators AND the entry appears at the bottom of the Roster Panel with the character&apos;s name, spawned indicator hidden, and active indicator hidden" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3035" y="110" width="300" height="100" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-add-character-to-roster-ac2-56" value="2. WHEN the GM adds a Character that is already present in the Roster THEN the Roster rejects the addition with user feedback explaining the character is already on the roster BUT no duplicate Roster Entry is created" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3035" y="220" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-add-character-to-roster-ac3-57" value="3. WHEN the Roster is empty before the add THEN the empty-roster placeholder is replaced by the new Roster Entry" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3035" y="302" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-add-character-to-roster-ac4-58" value="4. WHEN the GM adds multiple Characters in sequence THEN each appears as a separate Roster Entry in the Roster Panel in the order added AND all entries have Spawned State false until explicitly spawned" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3035" y="362" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-add-character-to-roster-ac5-59" value="5. WHEN the added Character has no identity or ability configuration THEN the Roster Entry is created normally; identity and ability configuration are not required for roster membership" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3035" y="444" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-add-crowd-to-roster-60" value="Add Crowd to Roster" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3445.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-add-crowd-to-roster-ac1-61" value="1. WHEN the GM adds a Crowd to the Roster via the Add Crowd action THEN each leaf Character in the Crowd (including those in nested crowds, expanded recursively) is added as a separate Roster Entry with Spawned State false AND all new entries appear in the Roster Panel in crowd-member order" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3355" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-add-crowd-to-roster-ac2-62" value="2. WHEN a Character in the Crowd is already present in the Roster THEN that character is skipped with per-character feedback in the result summary AND the remaining characters in the crowd are still added BUT no duplicate Roster Entries are created" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3355" y="206" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-add-crowd-to-roster-ac3-63" value="3. WHEN the Crowd contains no Characters (empty crowd) THEN the Add Crowd action completes with feedback that no entries were added BUT no error is raised" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3355" y="302" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-add-crowd-to-roster-ac4-64" value="4. WHEN the Crowd contains nested Crowds THEN leaf Characters from all nesting levels are added as Roster Entries AND the nested crowd structure itself does not appear in the Roster; only individual characters are listed" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3355" y="370" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-add-crowd-to-roster-ac5-65" value="5. WHEN all Characters in the Crowd are already on the Roster THEN the Add Crowd action completes with feedback that all members were already present BUT the Roster is unchanged" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3355" y="452" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-spawn-character-to-desktop-from-roster-66" value="Spawn Character to Desktop from Roster" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3765.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-spawn-character-to-desktop-from-roster-ac1-67" value="1. WHEN the GM selects a Roster Entry and triggers the Spawn action in the Roster Panel THEN the Game Bridge issues a spawn NPC command for that character AND the Roster Entry&apos;s Spawned State is set to true AND a Character Overlay for that character appears in the Desktop Overlay at the character&apos;s initial in-game position" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3675" y="110" width="300" height="100" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-spawn-character-to-desktop-from-roster-ac2-68" value="2. WHEN the character&apos;s Spawned State is already true when Spawn is triggered THEN the spawn action is a no-op with user feedback that the character is already in game BUT no duplicate Spawned NPC is created" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3675" y="220" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-spawn-character-to-desktop-from-roster-ac3-69" value="3. WHEN the Game Bridge fails to complete the spawn command THEN the Roster Entry&apos;s Spawned State remains false AND no Character Overlay is added to the Desktop Overlay AND the GM sees an error signal in the Roster Panel" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3675" y="302" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-spawn-character-to-desktop-from-roster-ac4-70" value="4. WHEN the spawn succeeds THEN the spawned indicator is shown on the Roster Entry in the Roster Panel AND the Character Overlay shows a spawned status indicator in the Desktop Overlay" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3675" y="384" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-spawn-character-to-desktop-from-roster-ac5-71" value="5. WHEN the GM spawns multiple characters in sequence THEN each spawns independently; success or failure for one does not affect the others AND each successful spawn adds a distinct Character Overlay to the Desktop Overlay" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3675" y="452" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-remove-character-from-roster-72" value="Remove Character from Roster" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4085.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-remove-character-from-roster-ac1-73" value="1. WHEN the GM removes a Roster Entry whose Spawned State is true THEN the Game Bridge issues a despawn command for the character AND the Character Overlay is removed from the Desktop Overlay AND the Roster Entry is deleted from the Roster" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3995" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-remove-character-from-roster-ac2-74" value="2. WHEN the GM removes a Roster Entry whose Spawned State is false THEN the Roster Entry is deleted without issuing any game command AND the Roster Panel no longer shows the character" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3995" y="192" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-remove-character-from-roster-ac3-75" value="3. WHEN the despawn command fails during removal THEN the Roster Entry is still deleted from the Roster AND the GM sees a warning that the NPC may remain in game" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3995" y="260" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-remove-character-from-roster-ac4-76" value="4. WHEN the removed character was part of an active Gang Mode group THEN the gang is deactivated for all members before the entry is removed AND the gang indicators are cleared from all remaining Roster Entries in that gang" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3995" y="328" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-remove-character-from-roster-ac5-77" value="5. WHEN the GM removes the last Roster Entry THEN the Roster Panel shows the empty-roster placeholder AND the Desktop Overlay shows no Character Overlays" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="3995" y="410" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-clear-character-from-desktop-78" value="Clear Character from Desktop" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4405.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-clear-character-from-desktop-ac1-79" value="1. WHEN the GM triggers Clear on a Roster Entry whose Spawned State is true THEN the Game Bridge issues a despawn command for that character&apos;s Spawned NPC AND the Roster Entry&apos;s Spawned State is set to false AND the spawned indicator is hidden in the Roster Panel AND the Character Overlay is removed from the Desktop Overlay" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4315" y="110" width="300" height="100" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-clear-character-from-desktop-ac2-80" value="2. WHEN the clear completes THEN the Roster Entry remains in the Roster Panel with Spawned State false BUT the character is no longer visible in game" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4315" y="220" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-clear-character-from-desktop-ac3-81" value="3. WHEN the GM triggers Clear on a Roster Entry whose Spawned State is already false THEN the action is a no-op with user feedback BUT no despawn command is issued" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4315" y="288" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-clear-character-from-desktop-ac4-82" value="4. WHEN the despawn command fails during clear THEN the Spawned State remains true and the Character Overlay remains visible AND the GM sees an error signal" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4315" y="356" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-clear-character-from-desktop-ac5-83" value="5. WHEN the cleared character was the Active Character THEN the active indicator is removed from the Roster Entry as part of the clear AND no character becomes the Active Character automatically" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4315" y="424" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-activate-characters-for-play-84" value="Activate Characters for Play" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4660" y="20" width="1290" height="615" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-activate-character-mark-as-active-turn-85" value="Activate Character (mark as active turn)" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4765.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-activate-character-mark-as-active-turn-ac1-86" value="1. WHEN the GM triggers the Activate action on a Roster Entry in the Roster Panel THEN that entry is marked as the Active Character AND an active indicator appears on the Roster Entry in the Roster Panel AND a distinct active status indicator appears on the matching Character Overlay in the Desktop Overlay" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4675" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-activate-character-mark-as-active-turn-ac2-87" value="2. WHEN a different Roster Entry is already the Active Character when the GM activates a new one THEN the previously active entry loses its active indicator AND the newly activated entry gains the active indicator AND only one Active Character exists at any time (unless Gang Mode applies)" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4675" y="206" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-activate-character-mark-as-active-turn-ac3-88" value="3. WHEN the GM activates a Roster Entry whose Spawned State is false THEN the active indicator is still applied to the Roster Entry AND no Character Overlay status indicator is shown since the character is not in game" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4675" y="302" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-activate-character-mark-as-active-turn-ac4-89" value="4. WHEN the Active Character&apos;s entry is already marked active and the GM activates it again THEN the action is a no-op; the indicator remains and no change is made" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4675" y="384" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-activate-character-mark-as-active-turn-ac5-90" value="5. WHEN the activated character belongs to an active Gang Mode group THEN all entries in the gang are also activated collectively, overriding the single-active rule" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4675" y="452" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-deactivate-character-91" value="Deactivate Character" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5085.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-deactivate-character-ac1-92" value="1. WHEN the GM triggers the Deactivate action on the Active Character entry in the Roster Panel THEN the active indicator is removed from that Roster Entry AND the active status indicator is removed from the matching Character Overlay AND no other Roster Entry is automatically activated" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4995" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-deactivate-character-ac2-93" value="2. WHEN the GM triggers Deactivate on a Roster Entry that is not currently active THEN the action is a no-op with no indicator change BUT no error is raised" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4995" y="206" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-deactivate-character-ac3-94" value="3. WHEN the deactivated entry is part of an active Gang Mode group THEN only that specific entry is deactivated; the other gang members retain their active indicators AND the gang mode itself is not automatically ended by deactivating a single member" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4995" y="274" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-deactivate-character-ac4-95" value="4. WHEN deactivation succeeds THEN the Roster Panel shows no active indicator on any entry AND no Character Overlay shows an active status indicator BUT the Roster entries, Spawned States, and gang membership are unchanged" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="4995" y="370" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-activate-crowd-as-gang-with-gang-leader-96" value="Activate Crowd as Gang with Gang Leader" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5405.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-activate-crowd-as-gang-with-gang-leader-ac1-97" value="1. WHEN the GM triggers Activate Gang, selects a Crowd, and designates a Gang Leader THEN all Roster Entries belonging to that Crowd are activated simultaneously AND each participating entry shows a gang membership indicator in the Roster Panel AND the Gang Leader entry shows a distinct leader indicator AND matching Character Overlays in the Desktop Overlay show gang status indicators" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5315" y="110" width="300" height="114" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-activate-crowd-as-gang-with-gang-leader-ac2-98" value="2. WHEN the selected Crowd has one or more members not present in the Roster THEN the Activate Gang action is rejected with an error listing the missing members BUT no partial gang activation occurs; no entries are activated" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5315" y="234" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-activate-crowd-as-gang-with-gang-leader-ac3-99" value="3. WHEN no Gang Leader is designated before confirming gang activation THEN the Activate Gang dialog prevents confirmation BUT Roster Entries are unchanged until a leader is assigned and the action confirmed" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5315" y="316" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-activate-crowd-as-gang-with-gang-leader-ac4-100" value="4. WHEN Gang Mode is already active on a different Crowd THEN the existing gang is deactivated before the new gang is activated AND the previous gang&apos;s indicators are cleared from all affected entries" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5315" y="398" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-activate-crowd-as-gang-with-gang-leader-ac5-101" value="5. WHEN the gang activation succeeds THEN the Gang Mode indicator appears on the Roster Panel header or status area AND all activated entries are treated as collectively active for ability and movement operations" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5315" y="480" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-activate-crowd-as-gang-with-gang-leader-ac6-102" value="6. WHEN a single Character is selected as both the crowd and the leader THEN Gang Mode activates with one member; the single entry shows both gang and leader indicators" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5315" y="562" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-deactivate-gang-103" value="Deactivate Gang" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5725.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-deactivate-gang-ac1-104" value="1. WHEN the GM triggers Deactivate Gang THEN all Roster Entries in the current Gang Mode group are marked inactive simultaneously AND all gang membership indicators are removed from the Roster Panel AND the Gang Leader indicator is removed AND all matching Character Overlays in the Desktop Overlay have their gang status indicators cleared" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5635" y="110" width="300" height="100" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-deactivate-gang-ac2-105" value="2. WHEN no Gang Mode is currently active when Deactivate Gang is triggered THEN the action is a no-op with user feedback BUT no Roster Entries are affected" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5635" y="220" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-deactivate-gang-ac3-106" value="3. WHEN deactivation completes THEN the Roster returns to single-character activation mode AND no entry is automatically activated as Active Character after deactivation" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5635" y="288" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-deactivate-gang-ac4-107" value="4. WHEN some gang members have Spawned State false at the time of deactivation THEN their inactive status is applied to the Roster Entry normally AND no game command is issued for unspawned members" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5635" y="356" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-interact-with-roster-on-desktop-108" value="Interact with Roster on Desktop" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5980" y="20" width="1930" height="519" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-select-character-on-desktop-via-mouse-click-109" value="Select Character on Desktop via Mouse Click" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6085.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-select-character-on-desktop-via-mouse-click-ac1-110" value="1. WHEN the GM single-clicks a Character Overlay in the Desktop Overlay THEN that Character Overlay displays a selection highlight AND the matching Roster Entry is highlighted in the Roster Panel AND any previously selected Character Overlay loses its selection highlight" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5995" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-select-character-on-desktop-via-mouse-click-ac2-111" value="2. WHEN the GM clicks empty space in the Desktop Overlay (not on any overlay) THEN all current selections are cleared AND no Roster Entry remains highlighted" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5995" y="206" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-select-character-on-desktop-via-mouse-click-ac3-112" value="3. WHEN the GM clicks a Character Overlay that is already selected THEN the selection remains; no deselection occurs on repeated single-click AND no Multi-Select state is entered" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5995" y="274" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-select-character-on-desktop-via-mouse-click-ac4-113" value="4. WHEN the GM clicks a Character Overlay while Multi-Select is active THEN all existing multi-selections are cleared and only the clicked overlay is selected AND the Roster Panel highlights only the matching Roster Entry" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="5995" y="342" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-multi-select-characters-114" value="Multi-Select Characters" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6405.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-multi-select-characters-ac1-115" value="1. WHEN the GM shift-clicks or ctrl-clicks a Character Overlay while another is already selected THEN that overlay is added to the current selection AND both overlays show the multi-select highlight AND both matching Roster Entries are highlighted in the Roster Panel" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6315" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-multi-select-characters-ac2-116" value="2. WHEN the GM shift-clicks or ctrl-clicks a Character Overlay that is already in the multi-selection THEN that overlay is removed from the selection AND the remaining selected overlays retain their multi-select highlight" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6315" y="206" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-multi-select-characters-ac3-117" value="3. WHEN the GM reduces the selection to one overlay using shift/ctrl-click THEN Multi-Select ends and the single remaining overlay shows a single-select highlight BUT the remaining Roster Entry remains highlighted" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6315" y="288" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-multi-select-characters-ac4-118" value="4. WHEN the GM clicks without a shift/ctrl modifier while Multi-Select is active THEN all multi-selections are cleared AND only the clicked overlay becomes selected (if a Character Overlay was clicked)" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6315" y="370" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-multi-select-characters-ac5-119" value="5. WHEN two or more overlays are selected via Multi-Select THEN a Context Menu triggered on any selected overlay applies to all selected characters simultaneously" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6315" y="452" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-drag-character-to-new-position-on-desktop-120" value="Drag Character to New Position on Desktop" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6725.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-drag-character-to-new-position-on-desktop-ac1-121" value="1. WHEN the GM drags a Character Overlay to a new position in the Desktop Overlay and releases THEN Movement Execution is invoked with the drop-point world-space coordinates as the destination AND the Spawned NPC is repositioned to the new location in game AND the Character Overlay moves to reflect the new in-game position" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6635" y="110" width="300" height="100" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-drag-character-to-new-position-on-desktop-ac2-122" value="2. WHEN the drag releases on a point outside the game world boundary THEN the drag is cancelled and the Character Overlay returns to its original position BUT no movement command is issued for an out-of-bounds destination" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6635" y="220" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-drag-character-to-new-position-on-desktop-ac3-123" value="3. WHEN the dragged character&apos;s Spawned State is false THEN the drag action is not available; the overlay does not drag BUT no error is raised" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6635" y="302" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-drag-character-to-new-position-on-desktop-ac4-124" value="4. WHEN the drag completes and Movement Execution reports a collision or blocked path THEN the Spawned NPC stops at the collision point AND the Character Overlay updates to the collision-halted position" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6635" y="370" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-drag-character-to-new-position-on-desktop-ac5-125" value="5. WHEN the GM drags a Character Overlay during an active Multi-Select THEN all selected characters are moved together with relative positional offsets from the drag origin AND each Spawned NPC is repositioned independently via Movement Execution" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6635" y="452" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-double-click-character-to-activate-126" value="Double-Click Character to Activate" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7045.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-double-click-character-to-activate-ac1-127" value="1. WHEN the GM double-clicks a Character Overlay in the Desktop Overlay THEN the matching Roster Entry is marked as the Active Character AND the active indicator appears on the Roster Entry in the Roster Panel AND the active status indicator appears on the Character Overlay AND any previously active entry loses its active indicator" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6955" y="110" width="300" height="100" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-double-click-character-to-activate-ac2-128" value="2. WHEN the double-clicked Character Overlay already belongs to the Active Character THEN the action is a no-op; the active indicator remains AND no change is applied to any Roster Entry" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6955" y="220" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-double-click-character-to-activate-ac3-129" value="3. WHEN Gang Mode is active when the GM double-clicks a Character Overlay THEN only the double-clicked character is activated AND the Gang Mode collective activation is replaced by this single-character activation" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6955" y="288" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-double-click-character-to-activate-ac4-130" value="4. WHEN the double-click occurs on an overlay belonging to a character with Spawned State false THEN the double-click is not interpreted as an activate; it has no effect AND a Character Overlay cannot be double-clicked if Spawned State is false" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="6955" y="370" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-sync-roster-selection-with-game-target-131" value="Sync Roster Selection with Game Target" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7365.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-sync-roster-selection-with-game-target-ac1-132" value="1. WHEN the GM changes the current target in the COH game client THEN the Memory Interface detects the target-register change AND the Roster Entry matching the newly targeted character is highlighted in the Roster Panel AND the matching Character Overlay in the Desktop Overlay shows a selection highlight" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7275" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-sync-roster-selection-with-game-target-ac2-133" value="2. WHEN the GM targets a character in game that is not present in the Roster THEN no Roster Entry is highlighted AND no Character Overlay shows a selection highlight BUT the application continues monitoring the target register" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7275" y="206" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-sync-roster-selection-with-game-target-ac3-134" value="3. WHEN the game target changes back to a character that is in the Roster THEN the previous Roster Entry highlight is cleared and the newly targeted one is highlighted AND the Desktop Overlay selection updates to match" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7275" y="288" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-sync-roster-selection-with-game-target-ac4-135" value="4. WHEN the game target is cleared in COH (no target) THEN all Roster Entry and Character Overlay highlights driven by target sync are cleared AND any GM-driven selection in the Roster Panel or Desktop Overlay is preserved independently" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7275" y="370" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-track-spawned-state-per-character-136" value="Track Spawned State per Character" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7685.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-track-spawned-state-per-character-ac1-137" value="1. WHEN a character is spawned from the Roster Panel or Context Menu THEN the Roster Entry&apos;s Spawned State is set to true AND a spawned indicator appears on the Roster Entry in the Roster Panel" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7595" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-track-spawned-state-per-character-ac2-138" value="2. WHEN a character is cleared from the desktop or removed from the Roster THEN the Roster Entry&apos;s Spawned State is set to false AND the spawned indicator is hidden on the Roster Entry" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7595" y="192" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-track-spawned-state-per-character-ac3-139" value="3. WHEN Game Done State becomes true THEN all Roster Entries have their Spawned State set to false simultaneously AND all spawned indicators are hidden in the Roster Panel" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7595" y="260" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-track-spawned-state-per-character-ac4-140" value="4. WHEN Spawned State is false for a Roster Entry THEN the matching Character Overlay is not rendered in the Desktop Overlay AND drag, double-click, and movement interactions are unavailable for that entry" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7595" y="328" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-track-spawned-state-per-character-ac5-141" value="5. WHEN multiple characters have Spawned State true simultaneously THEN each tracks its own flag independently AND each shows its own spawned indicator in the Roster Panel and Character Overlay in the Desktop Overlay" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7595" y="410" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-desktop-context-menu-actions-142" value="Desktop Context Menu Actions" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#e1d5e7;strokeColor=#9673a6;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=11;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7940" y="20" width="2890" height="519" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-spawn-character-via-context-menu-143" value="Spawn Character via Context Menu" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8045.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-spawn-character-via-context-menu-ac1-144" value="1. WHEN the GM right-clicks a Character Overlay whose Spawned State is false THEN the Context Menu shows the Spawn action as an available option" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7955" y="110" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-spawn-character-via-context-menu-ac2-145" value="2. WHEN the GM selects Spawn from the Context Menu THEN the Game Bridge issues a spawn command for the target character AND the Roster Entry&apos;s Spawned State is set to true AND the Character Overlay updates to show a spawned status indicator" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7955" y="178" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-spawn-character-via-context-menu-ac3-146" value="3. WHEN the Context Menu is opened on a Character Overlay whose Spawned State is true THEN the Spawn action is not shown in the menu BUT all other applicable actions remain visible" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7955" y="260" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-spawn-character-via-context-menu-ac4-147" value="4. WHEN the spawn command via Context Menu fails THEN the Roster Entry&apos;s Spawned State remains false AND the Character Overlay does not update AND the GM sees an error signal" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="7955" y="328" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-place-character-at-location-148" value="Place Character at Location" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8365.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-place-character-at-location-ac1-149" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Place at Location from the Context Menu on a spawned character THEN the Mouse XYZ Position at the time of the action is read from the Game State Query AND Movement Execution is invoked to move the character to those world-space coordinates AND the Character Overlay repositions in the Desktop Overlay to reflect the new location" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8275" y="110" width="300" height="100" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-place-character-at-location-ac2-150" value="2. WHEN the Mouse XYZ Position is unavailable (game window not focused) THEN the Place at Location action surfaces a feedback message indicating the position cannot be determined BUT no movement command is issued and the character remains at its current location" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8275" y="220" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-place-character-at-location-ac3-151" value="3. WHEN the target character&apos;s Spawned State is false THEN the Place at Location action is not available in the Context Menu" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8275" y="316" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-place-character-at-location-ac4-152" value="4. WHEN Movement Execution detects a collision at the destination THEN the character is placed at the closest valid position on the approach path AND the Character Overlay reflects the halted position AND the GM sees placement feedback indicating the adjusted destination" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8275" y="376" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-save-character-position-153" value="Save Character Position" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8685.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-save-character-position-ac1-154" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Save Position from the Context Menu on a spawned character THEN the Memory Interface reads the character&apos;s current X/Y/Z position AND the coordinates are stored as the Saved Character Position on the Roster Entry AND the GM sees confirmation that the position has been saved" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8595" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-save-character-position-ac2-155" value="2. WHEN a Saved Character Position already exists for the character THEN it is overwritten by the new position on Save Position AND the previously saved coordinates are discarded" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8595" y="206" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-save-character-position-ac3-156" value="3. WHEN the Memory Interface cannot read the character&apos;s position THEN the save fails and no Saved Character Position is written AND the GM sees an error signal BUT any prior Saved Character Position for the character is not overwritten on failure" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8595" y="274" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-save-character-position-ac4-157" value="4. WHEN the target character&apos;s Spawned State is false THEN Save Position is not available in the Context Menu BUT any previously Saved Character Position remains intact" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8595" y="370" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-save-character-position-ac5-158" value="5. WHEN the save succeeds THEN the Saved Character Position is available for subsequent Place at Location or restore operations" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8595" y="438" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-move-camera-to-target-character-159" value="Move Camera to Target Character" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9005.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-move-camera-to-target-character-ac1-160" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Move Camera to Target from the Context Menu on a spawned character THEN the Camera Rig is directed to move to the target character&apos;s current in-game position AND the camera view in the COH game world updates to frame the target character" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8915" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-move-camera-to-target-character-ac2-161" value="2. WHEN the Camera Rig is not active (not deployed) THEN the Move Camera to Target action surfaces a feedback message that the camera rig is unavailable BUT no camera movement command is issued" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8915" y="206" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-move-camera-to-target-character-ac3-162" value="3. WHEN the target character&apos;s Spawned State is false THEN Move Camera to Target is not available in the Context Menu" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8915" y="288" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-move-camera-to-target-character-ac4-163" value="4. WHEN the move completes THEN the Camera Rig is positioned at or near the character AND subsequent maneuver or follow operations use the new camera position" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="8915" y="348" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-move-target-character-to-camera-164" value="Move Target Character to Camera" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9325.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-move-target-character-to-camera-ac1-165" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Move Target to Camera from the Context Menu on a spawned character THEN the Camera Rig&apos;s current world-space position is read AND Movement Execution is invoked to move the character to the camera position AND the Character Overlay repositions in the Desktop Overlay to reflect the new location" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9235" y="110" width="300" height="100" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-move-target-character-to-camera-ac2-166" value="2. WHEN the Camera Rig is not active THEN the Move Target to Camera action surfaces a feedback message BUT no movement command is issued and the character&apos;s position is unchanged" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9235" y="220" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-move-target-character-to-camera-ac3-167" value="3. WHEN the movement to camera position is blocked by a collision THEN the character stops at the collision point AND the Character Overlay reflects the halted position" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9235" y="288" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-move-target-character-to-camera-ac4-168" value="4. WHEN the target character&apos;s Spawned State is false THEN Move Target to Camera is not available in the Context Menu" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9235" y="356" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-reset-character-orientation-via-context-menu-169" value="Reset Character Orientation via Context Menu" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9645.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-reset-character-orientation-via-context-menu-ac1-170" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Reset Orientation from the Context Menu on a spawned character THEN Movement Execution writes the identity rotation matrix to process memory for that character AND the character&apos;s facing direction is reset to the default north-facing orientation in the COH game world" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9555" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-reset-character-orientation-via-context-menu-ac2-171" value="2. WHEN the reset completes THEN the character is facing the default direction and the orientation change is visible in game AND no position change occurs; only the facing direction changes" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9555" y="206" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-reset-character-orientation-via-context-menu-ac3-172" value="3. WHEN the target character&apos;s Spawned State is false THEN Reset Orientation is not available in the Context Menu" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9555" y="274" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-reset-character-orientation-via-context-menu-ac4-173" value="4. WHEN Movement Execution fails to write the rotation THEN the facing direction is unchanged AND the GM sees an error signal in the Context Menu action feedback" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9555" y="334" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-maneuver-character-with-camera-via-context-menu-174" value="Maneuver Character with Camera via Context Menu" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9965.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-maneuver-character-with-camera-via-context-menu-ac1-175" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Maneuver with Camera from the Context Menu on a spawned character THEN maneuver-with-camera mode is activated for that character AND subsequent movement commands drive the character in the Camera Rig&apos;s current facing direction" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9875" y="110" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-maneuver-character-with-camera-via-context-menu-ac2-176" value="2. WHEN the Camera Rig is not active THEN the Maneuver with Camera action surfaces a feedback message and is not applied BUT no error state is entered" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9875" y="192" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-maneuver-character-with-camera-via-context-menu-ac3-177" value="3. WHEN maneuver-with-camera mode is already active for the character THEN selecting the action again deactivates the mode AND movement commands revert to fixed-destination mode" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9875" y="260" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-maneuver-character-with-camera-via-context-menu-ac4-178" value="4. WHEN the target character&apos;s Spawned State is false THEN Maneuver with Camera is not available in the Context Menu" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9875" y="328" width="300" height="50" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-maneuver-character-with-camera-via-context-menu-ac5-179" value="5. WHEN maneuver-with-camera mode is active and the GM moves the character THEN Movement Execution computes the destination from the Camera Rig&apos;s facing direction at the time of each movement command" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="9875" y="388" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-activate-character-option-via-context-menu-180" value="Activate Character Option via Context Menu" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10285.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-activate-character-option-via-context-menu-ac1-181" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Activate Option from the Context Menu on a Roster Entry THEN that Roster Entry is marked as the Active Character AND the active indicator appears on the Roster Entry in the Roster Panel AND any previously active entry loses its indicator" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10195" y="110" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-activate-character-option-via-context-menu-ac2-182" value="2. WHEN the character targeted by the Context Menu is already the Active Character THEN the Activate Option action is a no-op; the active indicator remains" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10195" y="206" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-activate-character-option-via-context-menu-ac3-183" value="3. WHEN Gang Mode is active when Activate Option is selected THEN the targeted character is activated individually AND the Gang Mode collective activation is replaced by this single-character activation" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10195" y="274" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-activate-character-option-via-context-menu-ac4-184" value="4. WHEN the Context Menu Activate Option succeeds THEN the outcome is identical to clicking Activate in the Roster Panel for the same character AND any configured default ability for the character may be played automatically if that behavior is configured" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10195" y="356" width="300" height="86" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-clone-and-link-character-from-desktop-185" value="Clone and Link Character from Desktop" style="whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;overflow=hidden;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;verticalAlign=middle;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10605.0" y="60" width="120" height="40" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-clone-and-link-character-from-desktop-ac1-186" value="1. WHEN the GM selects Clone-Link from the Context Menu on a Roster Entry THEN a clone-link operation is performed: a new Character is created as a linked copy of the original in the crowd library AND the new Character is added to the same Crowd as the original AND a new Roster Entry for the cloned character is created in the Roster with Spawned State false" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10515" y="110" width="300" height="100" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-clone-and-link-character-from-desktop-ac2-187" value="2. WHEN the clone-link completes THEN the new Roster Entry appears in the Roster Panel below the original AND the new Character is visible as a linked member in the crowd library" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10515" y="220" width="300" height="58" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-clone-and-link-character-from-desktop-ac3-188" value="3. WHEN the crowd library is unavailable or saving fails during clone-link THEN the new character is not created and no new Roster Entry is added AND the GM sees an error signal BUT the original Roster Entry and its Character are unchanged" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10515" y="288" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-clone-and-link-character-from-desktop-ac4-189" value="4. WHEN the cloned character&apos;s name would duplicate an existing name in the target Crowd THEN the application appends a copy suffix (e.g. &quot;Guard (Copy)&quot;) to make the name unique AND the new Roster Entry reflects the unique name" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10515" y="370" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="inc5-clone-and-link-character-from-desktop-ac5-190" value="5. WHEN the GM later modifies the original or the linked copy in the crowd library THEN the modification is reflected in all crowds where either appears, because they are linked members sharing the same underlying data" style="fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cccccc;rounded=1;arcSize=8;whiteSpace=wrap;html=0;fontSize=9;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=4;spacingRight=6;spacingBottom=4;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="10515" y="452" width="300" height="72" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>